3"], "concepts": ["60e40fd4f1ef260f84ed1e41"], "question": {"text": "The time period of a satellite of earth is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>24</mn></math> hours. If the separation between the earth and the satellite is decreased to one fourth of the previous value, then its new time period will become."}, "options": [{"id": "766732", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math>&nbsp;hours", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f7f2ee0e063d9290193"}, {"id": "3e4fd2", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn></math>&nbsp;hours", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f7f2ee0e063d9290194"}, {"id": "7551fb", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12</mn></math>&nbsp;hours", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f7f2ee0e063d9290195"}, {"id": "8c24f0", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math>&nbsp;hours", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f7f2ee0e063d9290196"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f7f2ee0e063d9290197", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfb0"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b6b"], "concepts": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52bb"], "question": {"text": "An object of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math>&nbsp;is taken to a height from the surface of earth which is equal to three times the radius of earth. The gain in potential energy of the object will be<br />[If, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math> and radius of earth <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>6400</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>km</mi></math>]"}, "options": [{"id": "6ab2e9", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>48</mn><mi>MJ</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f7f2ee0e063d9290198"}, {"id": "62cd37", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>24</mn><mi>MJ</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f7f2ee0e063d9290199"}, {"id": "6752b0", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>36</mn><mi>MJ</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f7f2ee0e063d929019a"}, {"id": "a350ed", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12</mn><mi>MJ</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f7f2ee0e063d929019b"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f7f2ee0e063d929019c", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfb0"], "topics": ["60e5671c499d1e49588f87fd"], "concepts": ["60e5671a499d1e49588f87c5"], "question": {"text": "Two satellite $A$ and $B$ go round a planet in circular orbits having radii $4 R$ and $R$ respectively. If the speed of $\\mathrm{A}$ is $3 v$, the speed of $\\mathrm{B}$ will be :"}, "options": [{"id": "1cddd2", "text": "$3 v$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f7f2ee0e063d929019d"}, {"id": "635c75", "text": "$6 v$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f7f2ee0e063d929019e"}, {"id": "84b313", "text": "$\\frac{4}{3} v$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f7f2ee0e063d929019f"}, {"id": "6e9013", "text": "$12 v$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f7f2ee0e063d92901a0"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f7f2ee0e063d92901a1", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfb0"], "topics": ["60e5678e499d1e49588f927a"], "concepts": ["6162faf16ed13040ec849361"], "question": {"text": "The weight of a body on the earth is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>400</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>.</mo></math> Then weight of the body when taken to a depth half of the radius of the earth will be:"}, "options": [{"id": "75cb54", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>200</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f7f2ee0e063d92901a2"}, {"id": "b96416", "text": "Zero", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f7f2ee0e063d92901a3"}, {"id": "702b9c", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f7f2ee0e063d92901a4"}, {"id": "f7c206", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>300</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f7f2ee0e063d92901a5"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f7f2ee0e063d92901a6", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfb0"], "topics": ["6117b60a478ae845c43c63f1"], "concepts": ["6117b607478ae845c43c62fb"], "question": {"text": "Two objects of equal masses placed at certain distance from each other attracts each other with a force of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi></math>. If one-third mass of one object is transferred to the other object, then the new force will be"}, "options": [{"id": "060522", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac><mi>F</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f7f2ee0e063d92901a7"}, {"id": "2e0e58", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>16</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac><mi>F</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f7f2ee0e063d92901a8"}, {"id": "504396", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac><mi>F</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f7f2ee0e063d92901a9"}, {"id": "02a0b1", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f7f2ee0e063d92901aa"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f7f2ee0e063d92901ab", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfb0"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4763"], "concepts": ["60e40fd4f1ef260f84ed1e41"], "question": {"text": "Two planets $A$ and $B$ having masses $m_1$ and $m_2$ move around the sun in circular orbits of $r_1$ and $r_2$ radii respectively. If angular momentum of $A$ is $L$ and that of $B$ is $3 \\mathrm{~L}$, the ratio of time period $\\left(\\frac{T_A}{T_B}\\right)$ is:"}, "options": [{"id": "952575", "text": "$\\left(\\frac{r_2}{r_1}\\right)^{\\frac{3}{2}}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f7f2ee0e063d92901ac"}, {"id": "26934d", "text": "$\\frac{1}{27}\\left(\\frac{m_2}{m_1}\\right)^3$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f7f2ee0e063d92901ad"}, {"id": "c70a5f", "text": "$27\\left(\\frac{m_1}{m_2}\\right)^3$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f7f2ee0e063d92901ae"}, {"id": "667150", "text": "$\\left(\\frac{r_1}{r_2}\\right)^3$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f7f2ee0e063d92901af"}], "questionLabels": []}], "markingScheme": {"_id": "608283e223cf4b3ad8f125e6", "title": "JEE Single Correct", "correctAttempt": 4, "incorrectAttempt": -1, "createdAt": "2021-04-09T08:45:27.797Z", "updatedAt": "2021-07-05T05:39:15.785Z", "__v": 0, "updated_by": "6042252509c5bf34e8a2f178"}, "maximumAttemptLimit": 25, "linkedQuestions": [], "createdAt": "2026-04-14T14:30:23.496Z", "updatedAt": "2026-04-14T14:30:23.496Z", "__v": 0}, "position": 0, "_id": "69de4f7f2ee0e063d92901b8"}], "bonusSections": [], "packDetails": [], "paidFeatures": [], "tags": [], "timeRestrictionSlots": [], "createdAt": "2026-04-14T11:15:55.500Z", "updatedAt": "2026-04-17T04:57:58.707Z", "testType": "PYQs as Chapter Tests", "isResumeBufferAllowed": true, "enableAccessibility": true, "maxAttemptableQuestion": 25, "analysisVideoThumbnail": "", "analysisVideoThumbnailDark": "", "shortTitle": "", "subjectDetails": [{"subjectId": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "title": "Physics", "shortName": "Phy"}], "testTimerType": "mm", "isMarkForReviewAvailable": true}, "temporaryTestDetail": {"_id": "6a4a1e2b9cbf3c6513039950", "testId": "69de21eb7e39d99b57bc5ab0", "userId": "6914cc9c4d7566258ee3a8fd", "startedAt": "2026-07-05T09:04:43.791Z", "lastAttempte